# Diagram test fixtures are compared byte for byte.
#
# `mindmap-diagram` Requirement 3.3 requires that saving a map ADP did not change produces no
# diff, which its tests check by comparing the serialized bytes against the fixture on disk.
# With core.autocrlf on - the default on Windows, and set in this repository - git would store
# these files with LF and check them out with CRLF, so the same fixture would have different
# bytes on a Windows machine and a Linux one, and the test would be measuring git's line-ending
# conversion rather than the serializer.
#
# `-text` tells git to leave the bytes exactly as committed on every platform. Replace a
# fixture only by committing what the authoring tool actually wrote.
*.mm -text

# C4 model documents are compared byte for byte for the same reason (c4-diagrams Requirement 3.1).
*.dsl -text
